        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "For the C parser, yes; the Vimscript parser is blocked by a full rewrite of the parser. It's good enough for the sort of simple vimscript we see in Lua injections or the command line, but it is nowhere near complete enough for parsing our Vimscript runtime, let alone vim9script (which shares the filetype, because this is how Vim rolls, and which several core members still need to touch).",
